@@ -0,0 +1,294 @@
+# GitHub-Grade PR Review Experience Design
+
+Feature: GitHub-grade PR review experience for the ForkMesh Qt client.
+
+Date: 2026-06-24.
+
+Approved scope: full signed review model.
+
+## Context
+
+ForkMesh pull requests are stored under `pulls/<number>/`.
+Each PR contains signed metadata in `pull.md`, a signed patch in `changes.patch`, and optional authored commits in `commits.mbox`.
+The Qt client already supports signed patch PRs, comments, reviews, line comments, merge, conflict merge, mergeability checks, check runs, and agent conflict sessions.
+`PullStore` currently stores PR conversation events as append-only markdown files named `NNNN-<type>.md`.
+`PullEvent` currently supports `comment`, `review`, and `line-comment`.
+`PullRequest::reviewSummary()` folds latest review state per author into `approved`, `changes_requested`, or empty.
+`MainWindow::buildPullsTab()` already creates Conversation, Commits, Checks, and Files changed sub-tabs.
+`MainWindow::renderSplitDiffHtml()` already supports side-by-side diffs.
+`MainWindow::renderPullDiff()` already supports clickable diff line numbers for line comments.
+The Cloudflare Worker and Flutter inbox code currently verify only the existing three PR comment event types.
+
+## Problem
+
+The current PR screen has useful mechanics, but it does not yet feel like a professional review workflow.
+Review state is partly buried in header metadata.
+Conversation events render as a flat list, so reviewers cannot distinguish top-level PR discussion from line-level review threads.
+Line comments use a modal prompt, which breaks review flow and makes comments feel detached from the code.
+There is no durable resolved or unresolved conversation state.
+There is no first-class suggested change model.
+The Files changed tab does not yet behave like a review workspace with unresolved badges, viewed state, and inline threads.
+The approval and request-changes actions exist, but they need stronger visual hierarchy and clearer consequences.
+Adding these behaviors only inside `MainWindow.cpp` would make the already large file harder to maintain.
+
+## Decision
+
+Build the full signed review model.
+Keep the existing PR event types readable for backwards compatibility.
+Add new signed event types for review threads, thread replies, thread state changes, and suggestion state changes.
+Add a small PR review model layer that folds raw PR events into review-friendly state for the UI.
+Use the existing Qt theme and Primer-style visual language.
+Turn the PR detail pane into a review cockpit with a top decision summary, strong tabs, a true Files changed workspace, threaded conversations, and gated review actions.
+Use append-only events for all durable review state.
+Use local settings only for personal, non-signed state such as viewed files.
+
+## Goals
+
+Show review, checks, mergeability, linked issues, unresolved threads, and agent conflict state at the top of the PR detail view.
+Make the Files changed tab the primary review workspace.
+Show file status, additions, deletions, unresolved thread counts, and viewed state in the file navigator.
+Replace modal line comments with inline diff-thread composers.
+Support top-level PR comments, line-anchored review threads, replies, resolve, unresolve, and hide-resolved controls.
+Support suggested changes as signed review artifacts.
+Enable safe suggestion application only when the client can update the PR branch or create a safe follow-up path.
+Make approve and request changes deliberate review actions with clear resulting status.
+Keep old PR comments and line comments visible.
+Keep cross-node verification compatible by updating Qt, Worker, Flutter, and tests together.
+Move review folding and rendering support out of `MainWindow.cpp` where practical.
+
+## Non-Goals
+
+Do not replace the existing signed PR storage model.
+Do not rewrite existing PR history.
+Do not mutate another author's signed PR patch without a new valid signature or a replacement PR.
+Do not require web-only review infrastructure.
+Do not build a full GitHub clone beyond the review workflow needed by ForkMesh.
+Do not make check execution mandatory before a review can be submitted.
+Do not make viewed-file state part of signed history.
+
+## User Experience
+
+The PR list remains the entry point.
+Selecting a PR opens the existing split layout with the list on the left and the detail pane on the right.
+The PR detail header should show the title, PR number, base, head, author, status, file count, additions, deletions, and agent cost when present.
+Below the header, a compact decision summary row should show Review, Checks, Merge, and Links.
+The Review gate should show approved, changes requested, no review yet, and unresolved conversation counts.
+The Checks gate should show passed, failed, running, pending, or no checks.
+The Merge gate should show clean, conflicted, unknown, or read-only.
+The Links gate should show linked issues and relationship count.
+
+The sub-tabs remain Conversation, Commits, Checks, and Files changed.
+Each tab label should include a count when useful.
+Conversation should show the PR opening card, top-level comments, review events, checks summary, linked issues, and the review composer.
+Commits should show the PR commit list with author, date, subject, short SHA, and changed stats when available.
+Checks should show the current checks table and selected log, with clearer empty states.
+Files changed should show a file navigator and a side-by-side diff by default.
+
+The Files changed navigator should show each file path, status, additions, deletions, unresolved thread count, and viewed state.
+Clicking a file should render its diff and preserve scroll position where practical.
+Clicking a diff line should open an inline composer under that line.
+The inline composer should allow a normal comment or a suggested change.
+Existing line comments should render inline below their anchor line.
+Resolved threads should collapse by default but remain discoverable.
+
+The review composer should have three deliberate actions.
+`Comment` posts a non-blocking review comment.
+`Approve` posts an approval review and updates the top Review gate.
+`Request changes` posts a changes-requested review and updates the top Review gate.
+If the PR is closed or merged, review actions should be disabled with clear disabled-state text.
+
+## Event Model
+
+Keep existing `comment`, `review`, and `line-comment` events unchanged.
+Add `thread-comment` for a new line-anchored review thread.
+Add `thread-reply` for replies inside an existing review thread.
+Add `thread-state` for resolve and unresolve actions.
+Add `suggestion-state` for suggestion accepted, rejected, applied, or stale state.
+
+Extend `PullEvent` with optional fields.
+Add `threadId` for the stable conversation thread id.
+Add `parentId` for replies when needed.
+Add `lineStart` and `lineEnd` for range comments.
+Keep `line` as the primary anchor for old line comments and single-line anchors.
+Add `suggestionPatch` for signed suggested changes.
+Add `targetPath` when a suggestion touches a file that differs from the anchor path.
+Add `appliedCommit` for an applied suggestion state when a commit was created.
+Reuse `state` for event-specific states such as `resolved`, `unresolved`, `accepted`, `rejected`, `applied`, and `stale`.
+
+The new event files should continue to use the existing `NNNN-<type>.md` naming convention.
+The current filename regex already supports hyphenated event types.
+Old clients should ignore event types they do not understand or render them as generic comments if safe.
+
+## Canonical Signing
+
+Do not change canonical strings for existing event types.
+Add type-specific content for new event types.
+`thread-comment` should sign `threadId`, `path`, `side`, `lineStart`, `lineEnd`, `body`, and `suggestionPatch`.
+`thread-reply` should sign `threadId`, `parentId`, and `body`.
+`thread-state` should sign `threadId`, `state`, and `body`.
+`suggestion-state` should sign `threadId`, `state`, `appliedCommit`, and `body`.
+The signed canonical prefix remains `forkmesh-pull-comment-v1`.
+Keeping the prefix avoids a parallel inbox route while still preserving type-specific content hashes.
+Qt, Worker, Flutter, and test vectors must update in the same implementation.
+
+## Review Folding
+
+Create a review model that folds raw `PullRequest` data into a `PullReviewSnapshot`.
+The snapshot should include the latest review state per author.
+The snapshot should include the effective review summary.
+The snapshot should include all top-level PR conversation items.
+The snapshot should include all review threads grouped by `threadId`.
+The snapshot should include unresolved and resolved thread counts.
+The snapshot should include per-file thread counts and unresolved counts.
+The snapshot should include suggestion state per thread.
+The snapshot should include check counts from action runs.
+The snapshot should include mergeability state from `PullStore::checkMergeable()`.
+The snapshot should include linked issue numbers from the existing reference-linking helpers.
+
+The model should be deterministic.
+Events should fold by file order and event timestamp, with append order as the tie breaker.
+If multiple `thread-state` events exist for a thread, the latest valid state wins.
+If a thread has no state event, it is unresolved.
+If a new reply is added after a resolved state, the thread should remain resolved unless the reply is an explicit unresolve event.
+If a suggestion patch no longer applies, the UI should mark it stale without altering signed history.
+
+## Suggested Changes
+
+Suggested changes are signed review artifacts, not silent mutations.
+A suggestion should store a minimal unified patch when possible.
+A suggestion may store replacement text for the selected range when a minimal patch cannot be built at comment time.
+The UI should always allow reviewers to copy a suggestion.
+The UI should allow authors to reject a suggestion with a signed `suggestion-state` event.
+The UI should allow authors to mark a suggestion as applied with a signed `suggestion-state` event.
+Automatic apply should be enabled only when the client has a writable checkout, the PR head resolves to a safe branch, and the current node is allowed to update or re-sign the PR.
+If automatic apply cannot safely update the PR, the UI should offer copy or follow-up PR behavior instead of pretending the suggestion can be applied.
+If a suggestion is applied by creating a commit, the `suggestion-state` event should include the applied commit hash.
+If a suggestion is applied through a replacement PR, the event body should link to that replacement PR.
+
+## UI Components
+
+Add a focused PR review model module under `qt_client/src`.
+Suggested names are `PullReviewModel.h` and `PullReviewModel.cpp`.
+The model should not depend on widget classes.
+The model should be unit-testable with synthetic `PullRequest` values and action-run summaries.
+
+Add focused widgets only where they reduce complexity.
+Suggested widgets are `PullReviewSummaryWidget`, `PullConversationView`, and `PullFilesChangedView`.
+`MainWindow` should keep orchestration, repository selection, navigation, and store calls.
+`MainWindow` should not directly own all review folding logic.
+
+Reuse `MarkdownEditor` for top-level review composition.
+Use an inline lightweight composer for diff threads so the diff context stays visible.
+Use existing octicons and object-name styling patterns.
+Do not introduce a new visual design system.
+Use the existing dark and light theme tokens in `Theme.h`.
+
+## Data Flow
+
+Loading a PR:
+
+1. `MainWindow::reloadPulls()` loads PRs through `PullStore`.
+2. The selected PR is passed to the review model builder.
+3. The builder folds events, linked issues, checks, mergeability, and viewed state into a snapshot.
+4. The summary widget renders top gates from the snapshot.
+5. The Conversation tab renders top-level timeline entries and review summaries.
+6. The Files changed tab renders file navigation and the selected file diff.
+
+Adding a thread comment:
+
+1. User clicks a diff line or range.
+2. The inline composer opens under the selected anchor.
+3. User writes a comment or suggested change.
+4. Qt creates and signs a `thread-comment` event.
+5. A writable repo appends the event locally through `PullStore`.
+6. A read-only repo submits the event through the existing inbox path.
+7. The selected PR reloads and the folded snapshot updates.
+
+Resolving a thread:
+
+1. User clicks resolve on an unresolved thread.
+2. Qt creates and signs a `thread-state` event with state `resolved`.
+3. The event is appended locally or submitted through the inbox.
+4. The snapshot folds the latest thread state and decrements unresolved counts.
+
+Submitting a review:
+
+1. User writes an optional summary in the review composer.
+2. User clicks Comment, Approve, or Request changes.
+3. `Comment` creates the existing `comment` event.
+4. `Approve` and `Request changes` create the existing `review` event with state `approved` or `changes_requested`.
+5. The review gate updates from folded author states.
+6. Merge remains independently gated by checks, mergeability, and PR status.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+Existing PRs with only old events must render correctly.
+Existing `line-comment` events should appear as single-message unresolved inline threads.
+Existing `comment` events should remain top-level PR conversation entries.
+Existing `review` events should continue to drive approval and changes-requested state.
+The Worker must accept and verify the new event types before read-only clients expose controls that submit them.
+Flutter must sign the same canonical strings for any new event type it exposes or forwards.
+Tests must include cross-language canonical vectors for every new event type.
+
+## Error Handling
+
+If a new event cannot be signed, the UI should not append it.
+If a local append fails, the UI should keep the composer content and show the error.
+If inbox submission fails, the UI should show that the event was not submitted and keep the content where possible.
+If Worker verification rejects a new event, the client should show a clear sync error rather than pretending the comment landed.
+If mergeability cannot be checked, the Merge gate should show unknown and explain that a writable checkout is required.
+If check data is absent, the Checks gate should show no checks rather than failed checks.
+If a suggestion cannot be applied, the apply button should be disabled with a specific tooltip.
+If a thread anchor no longer exists in the diff, the thread should appear in a file-level "outdated" section.
+
+## Testing
+
+Add Qt unit tests for new `PullEvent` canonical strings.
+Add Worker Python tests for the same canonical strings.
+Add Flutter service tests or source-level tests for the same canonical strings.
+Add `PullStore` round-trip tests for `thread-comment`, `thread-reply`, `thread-state`, and `suggestion-state`.
+Add review model tests that fold approvals, changes requested, unresolved threads, resolved threads, and suggestion state.
+Add model tests that treat old `line-comment` events as visible inline discussions.
+Add UI smoke coverage for selecting a PR, switching tabs, opening Files changed, and showing top summary gates.
+Add a window-size regression test for the PR detail view so buttons, tab labels, and summary gates do not overlap.
+Add a manual QA path that opens a real PR fixture with comments, reviews, checks, and a side-by-side diff.
+Run `cd qt_client && ./run.sh test`.
+Run Worker crypto tests if the Worker canonical verification changes.
+Run Flutter tests if Flutter signing changes.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+A reviewer can determine PR readiness from the top summary without reading the whole thread.
+The PR detail view has clear Conversation, Commits, Checks, and Files changed tabs.
+The Files changed tab defaults to side-by-side diff and allows unified mode through the existing preference.
+A reviewer can create an inline thread without a modal dialog.
+A reviewer can reply to a thread.
+A reviewer can resolve and unresolve a thread.
+Resolved threads can be hidden and rediscovered.
+Unresolved thread counts appear in the top summary and file navigator.
+A reviewer can leave a suggested change.
+Suggested changes render as distinct review artifacts.
+Suggestion copy, reject, mark applied, and safe apply states are clear.
+Approve and request changes update the top review gate.
+Existing comments, reviews, and line comments still render correctly.
+Read-only clients can submit supported review events through the relay inbox once Worker verification supports them.
+The Qt, Worker, and Flutter signing behavior stays byte-compatible where each surface supports the event.
+The Qt test suite passes.
+
+## Implementation Order
+
+First, add the signed event model and cross-language canonical tests.
+Second, add the review folding model and unit tests.
+Third, replace the PR detail summary and tab counts with the folded snapshot.
+Fourth, upgrade the Files changed view with file status, unresolved badges, viewed state, and inline thread rendering.
+Fifth, add inline compose, replies, resolve, unresolve, and hide-resolved controls.
+Sixth, add suggested changes rendering and safe suggestion state actions.
+Seventh, polish approval and request-changes UI states.
+Eighth, run Qt, Worker, Flutter, and manual review QA.
+
+## Future Work
+
+Batch review submission can be added later if reviewers need draft comments before publishing.
+Reviewer assignment can be added later if ForkMesh introduces ownership or codeowner metadata.
+Required checks can be added later if repositories define merge policies.
+Stacked PR awareness can be added later if ForkMesh introduces PR dependencies.
-- 
